<!--
  Sigils. Suggestion 2.1, and DESIGN.md section 4's "sigils implanted in the wrists".

  A sigil is the Society's paperwork, written into the hand: a mark that says what
  Color the registries have this person down as. It does nothing by itself. It is
  visible in the health tab, it is lost with the hand, and it is what the Society
  checks when it checks.

  THE LIE A CARVED PAWN CARRIES. RR_CasteIdentity.ColorOf reads GENES, so a carved
  Gold passes socially - the ladder thought, the razor law, the titles all see a
  Gold. The sigil is the other answer: a carved Red still has a Red sigil until a
  Carver forges a new one. The two places the Society reads the paper rather than
  the body are the census caravan (TraderKinds_RimRising.xml) and the Lurcher hunt
  (2.2) - both C#, both in docs/Opus-Notes.md. Until that code exists the sigil is a
  mark in the health tab and a surgery, which is still the legible half.

  WHO GETS ONE. Every pawn generated for the Society, the Rim Dominion and the two
  merchant houses, matching their birth Color, via a PawnGenerator postfix in
  Source/RimRising/Sigils.cs (UNBUILT). The tribes and the Ascomanni have none - the
  Society never filed them. The Rising's pawns keep whatever they were born with.

  STRUCTURE. Hediffs: one per base Color, each a bare marker with no stages, the
  way vanilla's cosmetic hediffs are; no hediffClass, so Hediff. Sub-strains carry
  the parent's sigil (a Lurcher is filed as Gray; a Bronzie as Gold). The forge
  surgery is RR_CarveBase's shape from Carving.xml - Violet-only via RR_CarverWork,
  a kit and medicine, CarveTargetExtension naming the Color - with a lighter worker
  (Recipe_ForgeSigil, in Sigils.cs) that only swaps the hediff. Cheaper and safer
  than a carving: the forgery is the easy part.

  Body part: the sigil sits on a hand. targetsBodyPart false and the worker picks
  the first hand, so an amputee with one hand keeps the mark on the other and a
  pawn with none has no paper at all - which is correct, and the Society would say
  so.
-->
<Defs>

  <HediffDef Abstract="True" Name="RR_SigilBase">
    <labelNoun>a sigil</labelNoun>
    <defaultLabelColor>(0.85, 0.85, 0.85)</defaultLabelColor>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <initialSeverity>1</initialSeverity>
    <everCurableByItem>false</everCurableByItem>
  </HediffDef>

